# Git remotes (Ensemble v2)

This repo has **two GitHub remotes**. When the user says **push to git** (or similar), push to **both** — team org first, then personal fork.

## Remotes

| Remote | URL | Use |
|--------|-----|-----|
| **`ensemble`** | `https://github.com/Ensemble-Digital-Labs/ensmeblewebsite.git` | **Canonical team repo** — push here first |
| **`origin`** | `https://github.com/giachinh1/ensemblev2.git` | Personal fork — push here too (keep in sync) |

## Default push behavior

When the user asks to push to GitHub / git (e.g. “push to git”, “update github”, “push hot git”):

1. Commit first if there are uncommitted changes (only when they asked to push/commit).
2. Push **`staging`** to **both** remotes:

```bash
git push ensemble staging
git push origin staging
```

3. Confirm on:
   - Team: `https://github.com/Ensemble-Digital-Labs/ensmeblewebsite/tree/staging`
   - Fork: `https://github.com/giachinh1/ensemblev2/tree/staging`

If they name a different branch, push that branch to **both** `ensemble` and `origin`.

## Other branches

```bash
git push ensemble main
git push origin main
```

## Branch tracking

- Local `staging` may track `origin/staging` — still push **both** remotes after commits.
- Org repo name is spelled **`ensmeblewebsite`** (typo in remote URL — do not “fix”).

## Troubleshooting

If the user says they don’t see commits on the team GitHub, check whether only `origin` was pushed and `ensemble` was skipped.
